🤖 AI Governance & Institutional Accountability

Project Overview

This project explores responsible AI governance, institutional accountability, human oversight, and evidence-based evaluation.

Research Question

How can institutions evaluate AI systems while maintaining transparency, accountability, and meaningful human control?

Objectives

- Define practical AI governance principles.
- Identify risks, limitations, and accountability gaps.
- Develop evidence-based evaluation methods.
- Document human review and escalation requirements.

Method

Use documented sources, explicit criteria, reproducible analyses, and clearly stated assumptions. Distinguish established evidence from proposals and interpretations.

Validation Plan

- Verify source credibility and dates.
- Test analytical methods where applicable.
- Record limitations and alternative explanations.
- Revise conclusions when evidence changes.

Scope & Limitations

This is an independent research project, not a certification or formal institutional audit. Conclusions depend on the quality and completeness of available evidence.

Status

Initial research framework — proposed; not yet validated.

